## vim ignore
# Swap. This file is core.excludesFile, so it applies to EVERY repository: a
# pattern that is too eager hides real source files elsewhere, and `git add`
# skips them silently. Vim names a swap file `.<name>.swp` (then .swo, .swn,
# ...), so these anchor on a leading `.`. The upstream GitHub template says
# `[._]`, but `_` is the DOS-only swap prefix; it also made `db/_schema.sql`
# invisible to git.
.*.s[a-v][a-z]
# keep vector files: the swap pattern above also matches .*.svg
!*.svg
.*.sw[a-p]
.s[a-rt-v][a-z]
.ss[a-gi-z]
.sw[a-p]

# Session
Session.vim
Sessionx.vim

# Temporary
.netrwhist
*~
# Auto-generated tag files. The ctags output is a FILE (universal-ctags is
# installed for vim-gutentags / tagbar), so it stays ignored; a DIRECTORY named
# `tags` is ordinary source layout (app/tags/x.py) and is re-included. The last
# matching pattern wins, so `!tags/` must stay below `tags`; and since git cannot
# re-include a file inside an excluded directory, it is the directory that has
# to be un-ignored.
tags
!tags/
# Persistent undo
[._]*.un~

